# ExtraVersion @VERSION@ - finds the extra (non-Amiga) version of a file

Ported software often has a version that doesn't fit the Amiga version
string: `0.3-Alpha_3`, `2.45.0-rc1`, a date or a git hash. **ExtraVersion**
reads a second string, `$EXTVER:`, that holds this original version next
to the normal `$VER:` string (never instead of it). It works like the
Version command: on programs, libraries, scripts and any other file.

ExtraVersion is an [OpenAmiga.org project](http://openamiga.org/?function=gitproject&name=ExtraVersion).
The source code, test versions and bug reports are at
<https://github.com/OpenAmiga-org/ExtraVersion>.

## Features

- Prints the name and extra version of a file; `FULL` adds the date and
  the comment, `VSTRING` prints the whole string for scripts (an empty
  line when there is none).
- `VER` reads the normal `$VER:` string instead, with the same options.
- `VERIFY` shows the string as found and each of its parts.
- Reads tags the way Version reads `$VER:`: upper case only, a string
  without name, version or date is skipped and the search goes on, the
  return code is 20 when nothing is found.
- No libraries needed.

## Installation

Double-click Install, or copy `C/ExtraVersion` to `C:`. Install puts the
documentation, `ExtraVersion.doc`, in `SYS:Documentation/C` next to the
documents of the other Shell commands.

## Contents

- `ExtraVersion/C/ExtraVersion`: the command
- `ExtraVersion/ExtraVersion.doc`: the documentation
- `ExtraVersion/Install`: the Install script

## Using it

Put the extra version string in your program or script, like this:

    "\0$EXTVER: Program_Name ExtraVersionString (dd.mm.yyyy) Comment\0"

    ; $EXTVER: My_Script 0.3-Alpha_3 (12.5.2014) First test

Then read it in a Shell, for example:

    1> ExtraVersion S:My_Script
    My_Script 0.3-Alpha_3
    1> ExtraVersion S:My_Script FULL
    My_Script 0.3-Alpha_3 (12.5.2014)
    First test
    1> ExtraVersion S:My_Script VSTRING
    $EXTVER: My_Script 0.3-Alpha_3 (12.5.2014) First test

    NAME,FULL/S,HELP/S,VSTRING/S,VER=VERSTAG/S,VERIFY/S

`ExtraVersion.doc` describes the string and every option.

## History

### 1.3 (20.11.2026)

- First release from the OpenAmiga.org GitHub repository. The version
  string is now a real Amiga version, 1.3 (1.2.0b read as 1.2).
- `VER=VERSTAG` and `VERIFY` are back: the 1.1 and 1.2 source code was
  never committed, so they were written again from the 1.2.0b readme
  and checked against the 1.2.0b command.
- Programs that contain the bare search string `$EXTVER:`, such as
  ExtraVersion itself, are read right: a `$EXTVER:` without name,
  version and date is skipped. 1.2.0b printed ` Extversion` or parts of
  other strings for them.
- `FULL` and `VSTRING` work with the file name in any position
  (`ExtraVersion FULL file` looked for a file called FULL).
- No extra version string: prints "Could not find extra version
  information" and returns 20, like Version (1.2.0b printed nothing, or
  `()` with `FULL`). `VSTRING` still prints an empty line.
- A missing file or a drawer gives the AmigaDOS error and returns 20.
- Without a file name it prints its own extra version.
- The whole version up to the date is kept (`file 001`, was `file`).
- Ctrl-C stops the search in big files.
- Install script, icons and new documentation.

### 1.2.0 beta (02.01.2018)

- New switch `VERIFY` that displays the parsed-out information.
- Test code left out of the release executable, for a smaller file.
- Leading and trailing white space trimmed.
- 1.1.0b (December 2017): new switch `VER` (`VERSTAG`), finds the
  `$VER:` string instead. Fixed one trailing space in the returned
  string when there was no comment. Corrected the name to
  "ExtraVersion" in various places, thanks TSK.
- 1.0.1b (December 2017): an `$EXTVER:` string at the very end of a
  file without a comment is found. Non-standard versions such as
  `0.3-Alpha_3` are read.

### 1.0 beta (26.02.2016)

- Most of the command rewritten from scratch.
- Test cases and more than 40 test files for good and bad strings.
- Works on both text files and executables.
- Compiled with the newly published SDK.

### 0.4 beta (29.05.2014)

- Options `HELP`, `FULL` and `VSTRING`.
- Fixed extra trailing characters read into the string.
- Fixed strings in scripts and other text files not being found.
- Many other fixes and improvements.

### 0.3 (12.05.2014)

- Alpha 3. Updated `ExtraVersion.doc`.
